-- make4ht build recipe for the EPUB conversion of the Gray Paper.

-- Render each amsmath display environment (align, align*, alignat, flalign, ...)
-- as ONE whole-environment SVG image instead of letting tex4ht slice every row
-- and cell (at & and \\) into separate images. The slicing is what breaks on
-- our custom \left/\right/\middle macros, producing the "Missing }/$ inserted",
-- "Display math should end with $$" and "\mathbf allowed only in math mode"
-- cascades (tex4ht bug #179; the maintainer-endorsed fix is `pic-align`).
-- Real xelatex still typesets and numbers the environment, so equation numbers
-- and \label/\ref cross-references are preserved. We append (rather than
-- overwrite) so tex4ebook's own tex4ht.sty options survive.
settings.tex4ht_sty_par = settings.tex4ht_sty_par .. ",pic-align"

-- The Gray Paper uses biblatex/biber, so a single compile is not enough:
-- compile once with the tex4ht instrumentation to emit the .bcf, run biber
-- to build the bibliography, then compile twice more so cross-references and
-- citations resolve.
Make:htlatex {}
Make:biber {}
Make:htlatex {}
Make:htlatex {}
